# Docker build context for api/Dockerfile and web/Dockerfile (both run
# `npm ci` fresh inside their own build stage, then `COPY . .`).
#
# Without this file every `docker build .` sent the ENTIRE working tree as
# build context — including whatever `node_modules` happens to exist on the
# host/runner at build time. CI job 6 ("Security") runs `npm ci` (to run
# `npm audit`) BEFORE its "Build image for scanning" step, so on a real
# runner that host `node_modules` exists precisely when the build stage's
# `COPY . .` would copy it — overwriting the container's own
# freshly-`npm ci`'d, correct-arch/libc `node_modules` with whatever the
# runner produced. That is silently wrong (glibc/musl and OS-arch mismatches
# for native modules like argon2 and the Prisma engines) even when it
# happens not to fail the build outright. It also made every image build
# transfer 500+ MB of irrelevant context (measured locally), which is the
# actual reason the "Build image for scanning" step was slow enough to risk
# the CI job's watchdog.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.git
secrets
.nyc_output
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
.superpowers
*.log
.DS_Store
Sample of Forms
